cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PARALLM: LLM-assisted, provenance-grounded parameterization for PyBaMM"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-beta.1"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bruhpika/ParaLLM-PyBaMM"
url: "https://github.com/bruhpika/ParaLLM-PyBaMM"
abstract: >-
  PARALLM (Parameters — not a problem anymore, for PyBaMM) is a research
  prototype for closed-loop, LLM-assisted parameterization and inverse
  estimation of physics-based lithium-ion battery models built on PyBaMM.
  It treats the LLM as an evidence interpreter and workflow orchestrator,
  not an oracle for electrochemical constants: numerical estimation, unit
  conversion, physical checks, and simulation are deterministic. The public
  beta includes a reproducible PyBaMM DFN baseline, PyBOP-based synthetic
  parameter recovery and identifiability analysis, provenance-tracked
  literature ingestion/extraction, and a v3 literature extraction benchmark
  (37 items, 3 repeated runs per experimental arm) with retrieval
  ablations. Synthetic recovery and literature-benchmark results are
  reported; independent experimental validation is not claimed.
keywords:
  - lithium-ion battery
  - PyBaMM
  - PyBOP
  - parameter estimation
  - identifiability
  - literature extraction
  - provenance
  - LLM
authors:
